 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. AB = AC [00] & DC = DB [02] ⇒  BC ⟂ AD [09]
002. BC ⟂ AD [09] & AB ⟂ AC [01] ⇒  ∠BAC = ∠(AD-CB) [10]
003. FD = FC [05] & FG = FC [08] & FC = FE [06] ⇒  C,G,E,D are concyclic [11]
004. C,G,E,D are concyclic [11] ⇒  ∠CEG = ∠CDG [12]
005. G,E,B are collinear [07] & ∠CEG = ∠CDG [12] & A,C,E are collinear [04] & C,B,D are collinear [03] ⇒  ∠(AC-GE) = ∠(CB-GD) [13]
006. ∠BAC = ∠(AD-CB) [10] & ∠(AC-GE) = ∠(CB-GD) [13] ⇒  ∠(AB-GE) = ∠ADG [14]
007. G,E,B are collinear [07] & ∠(AB-GE) = ∠ADG [14] ⇒  ∠BGD = ∠BAD [15]
008. ∠BGD = ∠BAD [15] ⇒  A,G,B,D are concyclic [16]
009. A,G,B,D are concyclic [16] ⇒  ∠AGB = ∠ADB [17]
010. ∠AGB = ∠ADB [17] & G,E,B are collinear [07] & C,B,D are collinear [03] & BC ⟂ AD [09] ⇒  AG ⟂ BE
